## 9. WARNING-FREEDOM CHECKLIST (all verified with `-D warnings`, both paths)

1. `self::` on every re-export in a `mod.rs`, `super::` on every sibling import — otherwise
   **edition-2015 E0432 breaks bare rustc only**. (Bare `rustc test5.rs` must not be given
   `--edition`; requirement (a) is literally `rustc test5.rs`.)
2. `_args`, not `args`.
3. No array `.into_iter()` anywhere (edition-2015 `array_into_iter` warning).
4. No `try` / `async` / `await` as identifiers (reserved in 2018+); no `panic!(non_str_expr)`.
5. Exactly one `#[allow(dead_code)]`, on `ProgressTracker::stages`, with the reason in a comment.
   No crate-level allow. No `#[allow]` on anything else.
6. Hand-written `Default` for both structs (deriving is impossible with `total = 100`) — trait impls
   are never reported as dead code, so they cost nothing.
7. No `[lib]` target; no `src/main.rs`; `[[bin]]` present.

